I am working on an app in Python that allows you to make notes/level of:
   rooms,
   monsters,
   items,
   traps,
   etc.

It is currently aware of the main dungeons to the required depth and 
the 'mines.  I am working on roughs for the levels that follow after. 
As for everything else, such as tracking special dropoffs (boxes, 
chests/level....), and all the tricky stuff with NH, that would aid with 
ascencion kits and such, it probably won't be implemented immediately. 
Or for a while.  All I wanted was a nice place to keep organized notes. 
  Click, click.

Right now, I call it 'Vadie' after a character I started the base 
scripts with who is no longer with us (yasd).

Like I said, this is being written in Python and will require your 
individual system to have Python installed, with TK.  Most *nix systems 
(on which I am writing this) have pre-existing Python binaries that will 
work easily, unless you hack wthout X.

It should work with Win32 but I am not testing in that environment at 
this time.
When I have something that works and I am happy with I will link 
r.g.r.nh to the scripts.

